### 4.3 Limitations and Systemic Vulnerabilities

**Verification Collapse for Edge Compute.** For purely generative robotics on edge compute, software transparency and behavioral monitoring degrade. The system relies entirely on hardware attestation, requiring silicon-level governance that may be technically infeasible for general-purpose hardware.

**Platform Firm Circumvention.** Large firms may establish operations in non-member jurisdictions to avoid deposit bonds. Conditional access mitigates but does not eliminate this risk.

**Ratification Chain Failure.** Domestic ratification failures can cascade, causing coalition collapse even when international incentives align.

**Budget-Breaker Commitment Problem.** The non-refundable sink assumes the ICB can credibly commit to destroying forfeited bonds. Institutional design must include constitutional constraints on ICB discretion over sunk funds.

