|  |         +---------------------+---------------------+                     |     |
|  |                               |                                           |     |
|  |                               v                                           |     |
|  |                    +---------------------+                                |     |
|  |                    |  ICB ESCROW ACCOUNT |                                |     |
|  |                    |  Total: $18M        |                                |     |
|  |                    +---------------------+                                |     |
|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------+     |
|            |                                                                        |
|            v                                                                        |
|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------+     |
|  |                    PHASE 2: OPERATION                                    |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  Robotic system operates. Safety performance y observed.                  |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+ |     |
|  |  |  y >= y_safe:                                                      | |     |
|  |  |  - Normal liability allocation                                     | |     |
|  |  |  - Bonds retained in escrow                                        | |     |
|  |  |  - No penalties                                                    | |     |
|  |  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+ |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+ |     |
|  |  |  y < y_safe (catastrophic failure):                                | |     |
|  |  |  - Proceed to Phase 3                                              | |     |
|  |  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+ |     |
|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------+     |
|            |                                                                        |
|            v                                                                        |
|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------+     |
|  |                    PHASE 3: FORFEITURE                                   |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  Liability allocation:                                                    |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  s_i(y) = proportional_share_i - phi_i * B_i                            |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  Example (phi = 0.5 for all):                                             |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  +----------------+     +----------------+     +----------------+         |     |
|  |  |  Manufacturer  |     |  Component     |     |  Software      |         |     |
|  |  |  receives      |     |  Supplier      |     |  Provider      |         |     |
|  |  |  share - $5M   |     |  receives      |     |  receives      |         |     |
|  |  |                |     |  share - $2.5M |     |  share - $1.5M |         |     |
|  |  +----------------+     +----------------+     +----------------+         |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  ICB retains: $9M as NON-REFUNDABLE SINK                                  |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+ |     |
|  |  |  SINK FUNCTIONS:                                                   | |     |
|  |  |  - Destroyed (deleted from account)                                | |     |
|  |  |  - Or committed to global safety infrastructure                    | |     |
|  |  |  - NOT redistributed to other participants                         | |     |
|  |  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+ |     |
|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------+     |
|            |                                                                        |
|            v                                                                        |
|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------+     |
|  |                    PHASE 4: INCENTIVE EFFECT                             |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  Ex ante, each participant faces:                                        |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  Expected loss from shirking:                                             |     |
|  |    phi_i * B_i * Pr(y < y_safe | e_i = e_shirk)                          |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  Expected gain from shirking:                                             |     |
|  |    dc_i/de_i * (e_i^effort - e_i^shirk)                                 |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  Efficiency condition:                                                    |     |
|  |    phi_i * B_i * Pr(y < y_safe | shirk) = dc_i/de_i(e_i^*)              |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  Result: Each participant chooses e_i^* = e_i^Pareto                    |     |
|  |                                                                           |     |
|  |  Budget breaking:                                                         |     |
|  |    sum_i s_i(y) < y (for y < y_safe)                                     |     |
|  |    This breaks the Holmström impossibility                               |     |
|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------+     |
|                                                                                     |
+=====================================================================================+
